A smart factory contains 500 sensors distributed across a 2 km area. Compare Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, LoRa, and MQTT-based communication. 
Which protocol or combination of protocols would you choose and why? 
Ans – For a factory with 500 sensors over a 2 km area, I would choose LoRa + MQTT. Wi-Fi and Bluetooth have a short range and would 
need many access points. LoRa can cover long distances with low power consumption, making it suitable for large factories. MQTT can then
\send the collected data from the gateway to the cloud efficiently. This combination is reliable, cost-effective, and ideal for industrial 
IoT 
